Folio 0.3.5 -- a PDF reader for AROS One x86_64
===============================================

Folio shows PDF files in a Zune window: continuous scrolling, a thumbnail
sidebar and the document's outline, zoom, text search, text selection and
copy, "copy as image", and a yellow highlight marker that is saved into the
PDF. It is built on the MuPDF library.

Third test release; see CHANGELOG for what changed.


WHAT YOU NEED
-------------

  * AROS One 1.3, x86_64. This binary is built for ABIv11, the ABI used by
    AROS One. It does NOT run on mainline AROS (ABIv1): a program built for
    one ABI does not start on the other.
  * Nothing else. MuPDF and its libraries are linked into the program; the
    system libraries it opens (intuition, graphics, cybergraphics, muimaster,
    asl, iffparse, utility, crt, stdlib) all ship with AROS One.
  * Memory: a page rendered at screen width takes 1-2 MB; Folio keeps up to
    six rendered pages plus thumbnails.


INSTALLING
----------

  Unpack the archive anywhere and double-click the Folio icon, or from a
  Shell:

      Folio file.pdf [page]

  The icon carries an 8 MB stack. If you make your own icon or start Folio
  from Workbench some other way, keep that value: a small stack crashes the
  font engine.


USING IT
--------

  Project menu   Open... (Amiga+O), Save (Amiga+S), Save As... (Amiga+A),
                 About..., Quit (Amiga+Q)
  Edit menu      Copy (Amiga+C), Copy as Image (Amiga+I), Highlight (Amiga+H),
                 Find... (Amiga+F), Find Next (Amiga+G)
  View menu      Zoom In (Amiga+=), Zoom Out (Amiga+-), Fit Width (Amiga+0),
                 Fit Page (Amiga+9); Ctrl or Amiga with the mouse wheel zooms
                 around the pointer

  Keys           cursor up/down scroll; PgUp/PgDn and Space by a screenful;
                 Home/End; cursor left/right previous/next page.
  Mouse          drag over the text to select it, across pages; the right
                 button over a page opens a menu with Copy, Copy as Image
                 and Highlight. Drop a PDF's icon on the window to open it.
  Sidebar        "Pages" shows thumbnails (click to jump), "Outline" the
                 table of contents. Drag the divider to resize it.
  Links          underlined; a click follows a link within the document, or
                 opens a URL through openurl.library when it is installed.

  Highlight turns the selected text into a PDF highlight annotation. Save
  appends it to the file (the original bytes are kept); Save As writes a
  new file. Folio asks before discarding unsaved highlights.

  Copy puts the text on the clipboard as FTXT with a CHRS chunk (8-bit) and
  a UTF8 chunk for programs that read it. Copy as Image puts the dragged
  rectangle on the clipboard as a 24-bit ILBM.


KNOWN LIMITS
------------

  * Rendering runs in the window's own task: a complex page freezes the
    window for as long as it takes to draw.
  * No forms, no printing, no annotation other than highlight.
  * Copy as Image: the ILBM is well formed, but MultiView on AROS One showed
    it blank in testing; other receivers were not tried.
  * Text copied to the clipboard is reduced to Latin-1 in the CHRS chunk;
    characters outside it become '?' there (the UTF8 chunk is complete).
  * Tested only on AROS One 1.3 x86_64 under QEMU.


LICENCE AND SOURCE
------------------

  Folio is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License,
  version 3 or later; see LICENSE. It links MuPDF (Artifex Software, AGPL)
  and MuPDF's bundled FreeType, IJG libjpeg, Little CMS, zlib, jbig2dec and
  OpenJPEG, and embeds the URW base35 fonts. Their licences are in the
  licenses/ drawer.

  The complete source is published next to this archive as
  Folio-0.3.5-source.zip and at
  https://github.com/tomaszstaniak/aros-foliopdf (release tag v0.3.5).
  That archive is the repository: it pins MuPDF 1.28.4 by commit in
  upstreams.json and carries the two patches in patches/, and its
  scripts/bootstrap.sh fetches and patches the exact MuPDF tree that was
  built (https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/mupdf).

